DECL	{"args":[{"name":"x","sort":{"sort":"track"}}],"body":{"add":[{"mul":[{"args":[{"var":"x"}],"measure":"kin_speed"},{"param":"reaction_time"}]},{"div":[{"mul":[{"args":[{"var":"x"}],"measure":"kin_speed"},{"args":[{"var":"x"}],"measure":"kin_speed"}]},{"mul":[{"lit":{"den":1,"num":2},"unit":"count"},{"param":"decel"}]}]}]},"contract":"The distance a road user would travel from the observation to a halt if it kept its current speed for a reaction time and then slowed at a constant deceleration: its speed at the observation (kin.speed) times `reaction_time`, plus the square of that speed divided by twice `decel`, in metres along its path. It is a quantity of the road user's own motion at the one observation, whoever or whatever controls it, and is zero for a road user standing still. Not denoted: the distance an actual later halt takes; the grade or the surface, which the caller states through the deceleration it passes.","definition":null,"id":"drv.motion.stopping_distance","kind":"quantity","narrowings":[],"params":[{"name":"reaction_time","unit":"second"},{"name":"decel","unit":"metre_per_second_sq"}],"residues":[],"supersedes":null}
